{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792349939,"nonce":"V3/XnADxL3UVNzIXirTCB9s5u14=","title":"Extension hooks, commands and contributions: IDE signals in, actions and tabs out","message":"Requirement from the user, 2026-10-18: RayScript should be able to receive IDE hooks and signals and use them. Example: an extension registers an action in a context menu, \"Preview\", for a markdown file; choosing it runs the extension, which parses the markdown and presents it in the main section as a tab.\n\nParts\n1. Signals into the extension. The editor sends `{\"t\":\"hook\",\"name\":\"file.opened\",\"data\":{...}}`; the script subscribes with `onHook(name, handler)` (or `ide.on`). The host tells the editor what is subscribed (`{\"t\":\"subscribe\",\"hook\":\"file.saved\"}`) so the editor sends only those. First hooks: `file.opened`, `file.closed`, `file.saved`, `file.changed` (typing, debounced), `active.changed`, `project.opened`, `selection.changed`.\n2. Commands. A script registers `registerCommand(\"preview\", handler)`; the editor runs one with `{\"t\":\"command\",\"id\":\"preview\",\"args\":{...}}`. A command is also in the command center, and can have a key binding.\n3. Contributions, declared in the `.rayext` so the editor knows them before the script runs: `contributes.commands` (id, title, icon), `contributes.menus` (location `explorer/context`, `editor/context`, `editor/title`, `tab/context`; each item names a command, and a `when`), `contributes.keybindings`, later `contributes.settings`. The form edits them.\n4. Tabs from the script. `mount(view, \"tab:Preview of README.md\")` presents the view as a tab among the open files. The editor tells the host when it is closed (`{\"t\":\"closed\",\"root\":n}`), and the host unmounts it. Tabs can be many, one per file previewed.\n5. Services the extension calls, answered by RayDE and checked against its capabilities, in place of mocks: `rayde.workspace.readFile(path)`, `activeFile()`, `root()`, `openFile(path)`, `writeFile(path, text)` (workspace.write), later `rayde.terminal`, `rayde.tasks`. A mocks file still overrides them in development.\n6. A markdown extension as the first real one (fixture and snapshot): written in RayScript, with the markdown parser in a script module, and a view for headings, paragraphs, emphasis, code, lists and links.\n\nDepends on: the Explorer context menu issue (the menu items are drawn there); rayscript-host (rayscript issue 648e334) gains `hook`, `command`, `subscribe` and `closed`; the language needs what a markdown parser needs of its string library.\n\nDone when: the markdown extension's \"Preview\" item appears for .md files in the Explorer and for no other file, choosing it opens a tab with the rendered file, saving the file updates the tab, and closing the tab unmounts the view; each hook and command has a test against the real host.","files":null}]}